4. Modified console file (Apache-2.0 Section 4(b) notice)
   docker/Dockerfile.to20s-v1 + docker/to20s-patch-v2.sh change exactly one line of
   server.mjs, a file belonging to the upstream console (/opt/sm75-workbench/console),
   from "timeout: 3000" to "timeout: 20000".  That modification is recorded as an image
   label (sm75.localpatch=gpu-probe-timeout-3s-to-20s), printed as BEFORE_SHA/AFTER_SHA
   by the patch script, and asserted again after the build.  The upstream base image
   tags are never overwritten.

5. docker/libnvidia-api.so.1 is NOT original work.  It is a component that ships with
   the NVIDIA display driver (tested with driver 580.173.02, 720104 bytes).  It is
   included in this repository purely so the P-State power management path can be used
   offline; that is a practical choice by this repository's publisher, not a licence
   grant.  It remains governed by the NVIDIA driver license, not by the Apache License
   above, and this project makes no claim that the NVIDIA license permits
   redistribution by third parties.  In the 0.1.7 line this file is mounted read-only
   from the host and is never baked into an image.  If you would rather not carry the
   binary, use the documented way-back:
     SKIP_NVAPI=1 bash docker/build.sh
     NVAPI=none   bash run/start-here-v1.sh
     and set power.mode = sleep in the profile (pstate otherwise makes the console
     refuse to start the engine).
   Its integrity is pinned by sha256
   4a199f9b259a1098ab9c01d31c67f882a2531a0fbb9c3595ad3d016c7d131d8c
   (enforced by docker/build.sh and run/start-here-v1.sh).
   See docker/NVAPI-获取说明-v1.md for how to obtain it from your own driver instead.

6. Model weights are NOT part of this package.  tools/flash-next-tested.sha256 is the
   official "tested" revision manifest (34 entries: 15 main shards + 10 plefp8 shards +
   9 other files) used only to verify a copy You already have.  Recommended public
   checkpoints are third-party quantized releases; they carry their own licenses and
   base-model terms, which you must review before use.

